WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.342
A useful practical takeaway comes from comparing
the two heterogeneous search procedures.

00:00:05.422 --> 00:00:07.230
The expensive NAS Prune method,

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:10.641
which repeatedly removes the worst block and fine-tunes,

00:00:10.721 --> 00:00:15.941
offers no consistent advantage over the far cheaper
NAS One-shot method that just takes

00:00:16.021 --> 00:00:18.621
the top-scoring attentions in a single pass,

00:00:18.701 --> 00:00:21.972
at least when good attentions are correctly identified.

00:00:22.052 --> 00:00:27.393
Attempts to tilt the mixture toward the strongest
attentions or give them more heads also

00:00:27.473 --> 00:00:29.525
failed to produce consistent gains,

00:00:29.605 --> 00:00:32.510
reinforcing that the cheap method is good enough.
